    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Is there any chance of implementing something like this in the future?\r\n\r\n* https://github.com/pogyomo/submode.nvim\r\n* https://github.com/anuvyklack/hydra.nvim\r\n\r\n### Short Explanation\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82c77fa3-f31c-403a-935b-c26912ab9ec5\r\n\r\nA key combination triggers a submode that temporarily alters the behavior of keymaps until explicitly exited. This can be very useful for actions like resizing. For example, pressing `<M-r>` could enter a submode where `hjkl` resizes the window separator, and pressing `q` or `<Esc>` exits the submode.\r\n\r\n### Caveats\r\n\r\nSubmode should override buffer-local keymaps. This means that when a new window is created, keymaps should be dynamically applied to it.\r\n\r\nTo be honest, I don’t expect this feature to become widely popular or a perfect fit for the mini-ecosystem. However, I hope you’ll at least consider adding or implementing it, as this repository is very well maintained and this feature could fill a gap for other plugins, such as https://github.com/mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Is there any chance of implementing something like this in the future?</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pogyomo/submode.nvim\">https://github.com/pogyomo/submode.nvim</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/anuvyklack/hydra.nvim\">https://github.com/anuvyklack/hydra.nvim</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Short Explanation</h3>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">keymodes.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/119845045/440147414-82c77fa3-f31c-403a-935b-c26912ab9ec5.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMwNDUsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjc0NSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTk4NDUwNDUvNDQwMTQ3NDE0LTgyYzc3ZmEzLWYzMWMtNDAzYS05MzViLWMyNjkxMmFiOWVjNS5tcDQ_.oeepr1HYYwGSylm8cQ6zLAMY2lUifr0QTtyp7p70_HM\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/119845045/440147414-82c77fa3-f31c-403a-935b-c26912ab9ec5.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMwNDUsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjc0NSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTk4NDUwNDUvNDQwMTQ3NDE0LTgyYzc3ZmEzLWYzMWMtNDAzYS05MzViLWMyNjkxMmFiOWVjNS5tcDQ_.oeepr1HYYwGSylm8cQ6zLAMY2lUifr0QTtyp7p70_HM\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">A key combination triggers a submode that temporarily alters the behavior of keymaps until explicitly exited. This can be very useful for actions like resizing. For example, pressing <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;M-r&gt;</code> could enter a submode where <code class=\"notranslate\">hjkl</code> resizes the window separator, and pressing <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Esc&gt;</code> exits the submode.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Caveats</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Submode should override buffer-local keymaps. This means that when a new window is created, keymaps should be dynamically applied to it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To be honest, I don’t expect this feature to become widely popular or a perfect fit for the mini-ecosystem. However, I hope you’ll at least consider adding or implementing it, as this repository is very well maintained and this feature could fill a gap for other plugins, such as <a href=\"https://github.com/mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim\">https://github.com/mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim</a>.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Is there any chance of implementing something like this in the future?\n\nhttps://github.com/pogyomo/submode.nvim\nhttps://github.com/anuvyklack/hydra.nvim\n\nShort Explanation\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    keymodes.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nA key combination triggers a submode that temporarily alters the behavior of keymaps until explicitly exited. This can be very useful for actions like resizing. For example, pressing <M-r> could enter a submode where hjkl resizes the window separator, and pressing q or <Esc> exits the submode.\nCaveats\nSubmode should override buffer-local keymaps. This means that when a new window is created, keymaps should be dynamically applied to it.\nTo be honest, I don’t expect this feature to become widely popular or a perfect fit for the mini-ecosystem. However, I hope you’ll at least consider adding or implementing it, as this repository is very well maintained and this feature could fill a gap for other plugins, such as https://github.com/mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim.",
